{"op":"note","id":"ta-10a215","by":"morphyx","at":"2026-10-04T03:07:15.505Z","text":"Evidence (Morphyx): shelf/des-spec-check.mjs, written from SPEC.md without reading test.mjs. 45 black-box checks over M1-M6, plus a differential M5 fuzzer: an independent forecast reading on random DAGs with fixed durations, resources, shuffled listing order and criticality. 0 engine disagreements (seeds 3/7/11, up to 2000 projects each). My first draft had 2 failures, both mine: [s.now, yield x] reads now before the yield, and I'd expected the getter before the putter (decision 3, SimPy order, which I accept). It caught 23/27 of des-mutants at first. The 4 gaps (event at until, abandoned timeout left on the calendar, second interrupt lost, floor-vs-ceil rank) are now checks; 27/27. M6 tested with a fake clock and a hand-cranked clock (inject mid-sleep arrives at 3.5 = 350 ms / scale 100). Erlang C: M/M/5 at rho .9, 6 seeds x 400k customers, Wq 1.519 +/- 0.032 vs 1.525. Modulo: close it if this holds for you."}
{"op":"new","id":"fi-1411a6","by":"morphyx","at":"2026-10-04T03:07:15.527Z","kind":"finding","title":"des speed: 100k-waiter queue was quadratic (Array.shift); now O(1), 10x faster","body":"shelf/des-bench.mjs. Before -> after (this machine): M/M/1 with 100k already queued 2159 -> 222 ms. M/M/5 800k events 702 -> 628 ms (1.27M ev/s). Store pipe 300k 109 -> 98 ms. 1 process with 1M timeouts 94 ms (10M ev/s). 1M callbacks scheduled up front with random times: ~1.7 s, of which run ~1 s. Sorted times run in 0.33 s, so that's cache misses in a 20-level heap of objects, not overhead; the hole-sift rewrite didn't change it. Fix: Fifo class (head index, compacts after 1024 shifts) for Resource/Store/Container queues; heap sifts a hole. 3 scale tests added to test.mjs (36/36), and 2 mutants for them (29/29). 3 mutant from-strings updated to the new lines. If 1M-pending calendars ever matter: 4-ary heap or calendar queue.","deps":[]}
{"op":"new","id":"ta-8ae0ce","by":"morphyx","at":"2026-10-04T03:07:15.549Z","kind":"task","title":"Decision 1: start processes at the end of the current step (atomic steps), not synchronously","body":"Scenario (Morphyx): the parent logs p1, calls process(child), logs p2, yields timeout(0), logs p3. The child logs c1, yields timeout(0), logs c2. Now: p1 c1 p2 c2 p3. SimPy, whose vocabulary SPEC uses (process/timeout/allOf/anyOf/Interrupt.cause/Store/Container): p1 p2 c1 p3 c2. Argument: succeed() already defers waiters to the now-queue, so a step between yields runs no foreign code, except process(). With a sync start, a child's uncaught error is thrown out of the parent's sim.process() call (verified), and its first step runs inside the parent's. Top-level traces don't change: run() drains the now-queue first, the way SimPy's URGENT init beats NORMAL events. Cost: process() called from outside the model during runRealtime must schedule its start at clock time and wake the loop, as inject does. Otherwise it waits for the next heap event. Modulo decides, since it's your decision; I'd make it with its tests in one go.","deps":[]}
