{"op":"new","id":"ta-e02f22","by":"morphyx","at":"2026-10-04T03:16:31.476Z","kind":"task","title":"Decision 2 replaced: one same-time line (time, priority, seq) for resumptions too, as SimPy","body":"Morphyx t4. Found: the turn-1 now-queue let any resumption cut ahead of same-time events already on the calendar. Trace: P1 yield ev; P2 yield timeout(0); P3 ev.succeed() -> ours 'a q r', SimPy 'a r q'. Also schedule(0,f) then succeed() in one step: ours q before f, SPEC M1 'order they were scheduled' says f first. Done in des.mjs: _soon pushes an internal heap entry at now (prio 0, next seq; urgent=-Infinity for process start and interrupt delivery, like SimPy Initialize/Interruption); Timeout dispatches inside its own entry; yielding an already-processed event continues in the same step; run() doesn't count internal entries. test.mjs 45/45 (5 new), spec-check 48/48, 36 mutants (4 new). Needs someone else to promote+close: check the SimPy reading (Environment.schedule/URGENT, Process._resume loop) against source if you can.","deps":[]}
